results/codex/codex_data_v2_verify3.md:46:**B1 — the new submit predicate erases real actions (training blocker).** `data/build_v2_mix.py:132–139` matches `keyboard` anywhere in the model-generated instruction, OR a bottom-right point. The Odyssey loop at lines 351–357 consumes that tap before intent consistency filtering. Raw adjacency and the second-tap cutoff work; they do not establish that the first tap is a submit. The actual-loop fixture `TEXT → “Tap to hide the keyboard” → result tap` wrongly consumes the hide action. The real executor probe confirms that the replacement `input_text` executes `type_text` plus one Enter, not an arbitrary toolbar or back-button action.
results/codex/codex_data_v2_verify3.md:48:The strongest published counterexample is **train/odyssey/5994133452263654/31**. Source step 26 types `Narcissus` into WPS. Step 27 taps **[686,499]**, described as an icon in the toolbar “above the keyboard”; it opens image selection. The classifier merges it. The published step-31 image shows the Download image picker with the Narcissus photo selected, while its retained source history is **22,23,24,25,26,28,29,30**: text entry is followed directly by controls inside the image picker, with no action opening it. Pressing Enter in the document is not that missing toolbar tap. The [pinned published picker](data_v2_cache/verify3_836e401958/visual/merge_04.png), [saved row/raw-step evidence](data_v2_cache/verify3_836e401958/blocking_examples.json), and [cached earlier step-28 picker image](data_v2_cache/verify3_836e401958/visual/old_wps_after_toolbar.png) make the omission reviewable. The last image is explicitly corroboration from audit 1, not a newly downloaded third-revision row.
