results/codex/dataset_viability.md:104:| TYPE | 2,419 | `input_text`; preserve its separation from Enter |
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:118:**3. GUI-Actor AndroidControl bbox — clean official-train IDs, weak incremental acquisition value.** The exact files are [`cckevinn/GUI-Actor-Data/androidcontrol_bbox.json`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/cckevinn/GUI-Actor-Data/blob/main/androidcontrol_bbox.json), **25,035,159 bytes**, and `AndroidControl_images.zip`, **49,306,113,518 bytes**. The full JSON contains **39,701 unique image rows**, not the paper's rounded 47K description. All recoverable IDs are official train, as shown above. Existing local AC screenshots can supply these same images, so downloading the ZIP is unnecessary.
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:120:Each row contains an image path, a human referring instruction, an assistant `pyautogui.click(x=..., y=...)` response with unit-interval coordinates, and normalized `bbox_gt` XYXY. All 39,701 responses use click. There are no trajectory histories, scrolls, terminals or answers. Converting a point to the 0–1000 grid is straightforward; converting an entire box into one point discards the box supervision. A normal point-output fine-tune also does not reproduce GUI-Actor's coordinate-free attention architecture. I found no invalid normalized boxes in the scan, but **400 boxes cover more than half the screen**; inspect them rather than treating large regions as precise targets. [Project and training configuration](https://github.com/microsoft/GUI-Actor), [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.03143).
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:134:| **`aw_mobile.json`, `mobile_images.zip`** | **31,860,297 + 2,325,202,926 bytes; exclude both**. Full JSON: 15,905 screens / 89,860 element references |
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:160:**Screen2Words.** The real host is [`google-research-datasets/screen2words`](https://github.com/google-research-datasets/screen2words), not an assumed HF mirror. `screen_summaries.csv` is **5,313,544 bytes / 112,085 rows**, five human summaries per **22,417** Rico screens. `split/` defines **15,743 train screens / 78,715 train captions**, plus dev/test. Select at most one summary per screen if ever used. The original README/tree contains no explicit licence file or dataset grant located in this audit; a downstream CC BY tag and Google's code-repository Apache licence do not settle it. **REJECT for current v2**, both for unresolved terms and low marginal value compared with direct ScreenQA. Conversion to a broad “describe this screen” answer is possible, but it teaches neither navigation nor precise task-state answers. It shares old Rico media, has the quantified AW-app overlap above, and needs the same image/readability checks. Estimate **3–6 h** if terms are resolved.
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:162:**Widget Captioning.** The real host is [`google-research-datasets/widget-caption`](https://github.com/google-research-datasets/widget-caption), specifically `widget_captions.csv` and the split files. The CSV is **5,007,978 bytes**. Parsing finds **61,285 rows** versus the README's 61,286 headline: **48,325 `rc` rows** for public Rico widgets and **12,960 `nr` rows whose privately collected screenshots are not released**. The public Rico portion spans 17,435 screens, with **41,221 train widget rows**. Counting pipe-separated caption alternatives as independent widgets would inflate scale.
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:183:The paper describes action re-prediction and grounding consistency filtering, which can make its labels useful. Sample outputs use long `<thinking>`/`<answer>` wrappers and an action space including point-conditioned `Write`, `Swipe`, seconds-valued `Wait`, and `Terminate`. These are not drop-in labels for short `<think>` plus one project JSON action: combined focus-and-write, raw swipes and wait duration lose semantics; only current screenshots are permitted here. Prefer the short/no-reasoning variant or produce a short causal intent, and preserve original source provenance through the rewrite. [Official project](https://github.com/GUI-Libra/GUI-Libra).
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:189:Actual train actions: **76,333 CLICK, 9,873 TYPE, 7,509 STOP, 4,310 SWIPE, 43 LONG_PRESS, 31 KEY_BACK, 54 KEY_HOME, 15 WAIT**. Pixels and screenshot dimensions are explicit. Observed dimensions are mostly 1440×3200 and 1080×2400, with 720×1560/1280 and landscape variants. Click, long-press, text, back/home, wait and genuine STOP can be mapped; swipes have the same loss as AMEX. There is no demonstrated answer/infeasible category. **11,051 episodes lack STOP**, so the last interaction is not a labelled completed-state screenshot.
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:195:**UI-S1 — reject until source provenance is restored.** [HF `mPLUG/UI_S1_dataset`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/mPLUG/UI_S1_dataset/tree/main) supplies `train_1000.jsonl` (**1,015,926 bytes**) and `images.parquet` (**3,470,098,427 bytes**). The full JSONL has **1,000 trajectories / 6,536 steps**, including 3,380 clicks, 782 swipes, 391 types, 376 opens, 372 waits, 227 system buttons, eight long presses and 1,000 successful terminations. The [official UI-S1 README](https://github.com/X-PLUG/MobileAgent/tree/main/UI-S1) identifies AndroidControl as its source.
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:197:Source pixels/bboxes and action histories can mostly be adapted subject to the same swipe/focus checks, but screenshot dimensions must be read from the Parquet media; this audit did not download that payload. Renumbered image keys prevent an official-episode allowlist. The 10 matching test goals are enough to reject a blanket “train-only, no leakage” claim, although not enough to prove screenshot reuse. **REJECT** for this evaluation setup. Recovery would require original-ID mapping or pixel hashes against official AC train/test before any selection. It adds little diversity to the existing source, and neither its packaging nor its public download resolves AC's licence conflict.
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:199:**GUIAct smartphone — a cheap fallback that must not be sold as QA supervision.** [HF `yiye2023/GUIAct`](https://huggingface.co/datasets/yiye2023/GUIAct/tree/main) hosts `smartphone_train_data.json` (**44,287,601 bytes**) and `smartphone_train_images.parquet` (**4,267,662,999 bytes**). Full annotation parsing gives **65,627 rows / 7,246 episodes**: 38,262 taps, 11,670 swipes, 6,560 inputs, **1,889 Enter actions**, and **7,246 terminal “answers”**. Specifically, 7,236 say `task complete` and 10 say `task impossible`; none supplies a factual screen answer. This corrects “all complete” without changing the conclusion about missing QA. [Audit](datasets_scratch/guiact_audit.json), [official GUICourse repository](https://github.com/RUCBM/GUICourse).
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:201:Its AitW-General-derived smartphone records include goals, history, pixel and normalized points, and image dimensions: 412×732, 540×1080/1140/1170 and 720×1440/1480/1520. The [paper's action-conversion appendix](https://arxiv.org/html/2406.11317) confirms that Back/Home were converted into taps on the navigation bar; their original action identity is therefore absent. A tap/Enter/type/terminal adapter is simple, but navigation-bar taps require the expected visible buttons, and raw swipes still lose target/distance semantics. Reconstruct causal history rather than blindly trusting formatted histories. No app/package field in these annotation rows permits a comprehensive AW-package count; recover it through AitW episode IDs or exclude unresolved examples. It was not collected as AW rollouts and is not AC-derived. Low resolution and AitW's repeated task templates constrain expected gain, while low download cost and Enter coverage are useful.
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:205:**Google AitW — the 494 GB figure is real, but it is not an all-or-nothing download.** The [official release](https://github.com/google-research/google-research/tree/master/android_in_the_wild) reports **715,142 episodes / 5,689,993 steps / 30,378 distinct prompts**, collected across eight devices and Android 10–13. The complete paginated GCS listing totals **493,592,603,661 bytes**. Subsets are General **13.62 GB**, GoogleApps **374.82 GB**, Install **35.96 GB**, Single **13.41 GB**, WebShopping **55.71 GB**, plus split metadata. [Recorded size audit](datasets_scratch/aitw_size_audit.json).
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:207:GZIP TFRecords carry encoded screenshots, dimensions, `current_activity`, episode ID, and actions. Important detail: stored touch/lift fields are **`yx_touch` / `yx_lift`**, i.e. y before x, even though descriptions may discuss x/y points. `DUAL_POINT` combines tap and swipe, and lacks the project's exact scroll semantics; text types into the focused field; back/home/Enter/status have direct equivalents. No factual answer labels. Actual full-release screenshot dimensions and AW-package prevalence were not enumerated in this audit; read the per-record dimensions and package-bearing activity before conversion. Collection predates AW; app overlap can still occur.
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:215:[Screen Annotation](https://github.com/google-research-datasets/screen_annotation) publishes train/validation/test CSVs of **16,993,478 / 2,904,772 / 5,323,569 bytes**, corresponding to **15,743 / 2,364 / 4,310 Rico screens**. The data licence is explicitly CC BY 4.0, with Rico media conditions. It serializes UI elements and attributes; emitting a whole screen annotation is not an allowed agent action. Deriving point queries would require source-box/type validation and app filtering, about **8–12 h**, without new images. **REJECT from v2** as a redundant and output-heavy auxiliary task; there is no demonstrated small-policy gain to justify that work.
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:238:2. **Invert finger movement into revealed-content direction.** For ordinary page scrolling, a finger swipe upward usually means project `scroll down`. Horizontal finger-left usually reveals content to the right. Reject drags, drawing, slider movements, pinch/multitouch, diagonal gestures and region-specific scrolls that the fixed executor cannot reproduce. Even accepted cardinal swipes lose length; do not call this exact gesture reproduction.
results/codex/dataset_viability.md:246:**Recommended v2 allocation.** This is an **80K total-row replacement mix**, not 80K additions to the existing ~99K. Local `results/data/dataset_verification.json` records a historical VM build of 99,216 rows: 74,595 high-level decisions, 13,573 terminals and 11,048 duplicated low-level rows over 13,573 episodes. That file is historical evidence, not a fresh enumeration of a live training store. Rebuild the selection manifest from current permitted train records before running.
