results/codex/final_write_report.py:66:The frozen GT SHA-256 is `1926a44e0ffa7940b28866907d28913a5bd4af38f5b67463798cec8b6df25e84`. Its 18,415 unique rows comprise **8,444 high nonterminal + 8,428 low nonterminal + 1,543 high terminal** rows. High-only has 9,987 rows. High evaluates 1,543 episodes; low evaluates 1,542. All GT fields also match the pinned Hub dataset's non-image columns. The local split file equals [Google's official split file](https://storage.googleapis.com/gresearch/android_control/splits.json).
results/codex/final_write_report.py:89:Newest directories selected at cutoff: base `run_20261116T190932199444`; LFM3 FT `run_20261117T030335477504`; 450M FT `run_20261117T022926194002`; matched GUI-Owl `run_20261116T231457945810`. The native sample is physically under `_smoke_guiowl_native/run_20261116T225639669685`, as its saved summary says. There are no duplicate task/instance files. Exceptions, NaN rewards and missing tasks count as failures. 450M base is absent and skipped.
results/codex/final_write_report.py:131:The pinned dataset `1c49e7d117bd109eebd976b04deefa708b0e2007` contains **99,216 train rows / 13,573 episodes**, **827 validation rows / 137 episodes**, and the **18,415-row test**. Reading non-image columns of every shard found **zero train/val/test episode intersections**, no duplicate row keys, no IDs outside official splits, and zero GT field mismatches. Thirty official train episodes are absent; the surviving stats cannot attribute all 30 to the AW-app filter. Independently reading the source mirror's train episode IDs reproduces the cards' **{mirror['official_test_in_mirror_train']:,} official test episodes in mirror train** claim.
results/codex/final_write_report.py:133:No positive split-leakage evidence was found. Limits: the AW-app filter is a name heuristic; screenshot duplicates across distinct episodes and pretraining contamination were not tested. 450M replay is recorded only as `/content/data/replay`, without an archived row/image roster or source revisions proving no MMStar/MMLU overlap. Run configs record model/dataset SHAs but loading code does not pin those revisions. There is no isolated replay ablation. AC train has **13,573 positive `complete` labels and zero `answer`, `keyboard_enter` or `infeasible` labels**; that supervision gap is consistent with, but does not prove the cause of, the observed failures.
