results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:92:Evidence: `train/sft_vlm.py:102–108,207,210` constructs and saves a processor with `size.longest_edge=774400`. `eval/general/eval_general.py:32` loads whatever processor is stored with each model and supplies no matched resize override. Both Qwen job files request 774,400 training pixels (`qwen35_2b_l4.json:17`, `qwen35_08b_l4.json:19`). The native [2B processor config](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.5-2B/blob/main/preprocessor_config.json) and [0.8B processor config](https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3.5-0.8B/blob/main/preprocessor_config.json) permit **16,777,216** pixels. The pinned processor maps the misleadingly named `shortest_edge`/`longest_edge` fields to **pixel areas**, so the training setting is valid; the general comparison is the problem. See `pass2/qwen2_vl_image_reference.py:159–169`.
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:163:These single-epoch calculations assume identical dataset/order/world size. The first change preserves row position, though dropout/floating-point grouping need not be bitwise identical. Changing the dataset or replay order invalidates even that conclusion. `lfm3_train_l4_resume.json:11–13` requests 1250/8/4; no saved checkpoint state was available to establish which change actually happened on its VM.
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:175:Training is not completely unprotected: pinned Trainer checkpoint upload includes the output directory, including logs, and separately uploads `last-checkpoint` (`pass2/trainer_reference.py:4389–4452`). However, uploads are asynchronous and a save is skipped while an earlier push is unfinished (`:4393–4395`); “every 100 saves” is not a guaranteed maximum remote lag. Restore downloads only `last-checkpoint/*`, not root custom logs. A new VM can subsequently overwrite the root JSONL log with only the new session's entries, although checkpoint `trainer_state.log_history` retains its own history. Logger `elapsed_s` restarts at zero on each process. The 450M wrapper waits until all evaluations to perform its final artifact upload (`vm_450m_pipeline.sh:40–50`).
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:303:Qwen3.5 patched:
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:311:| Qwen3.5 patched | Empty closed think block | Opens `<think>\n` | Empty closed think block | On yes; default/off no for nonempty intent |
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:313:Qwen's training assistant branch always renders the supplied reasoning; it does **not** need an `enable_thinking=True` training kwarg for this full-conversation dataset. The absence of that kwarg in `SFTTrainer` is therefore **not** a masking bug. Inference does need explicit true to continue the trained nonempty thought prefix; `generate.py:86` supplies it for the configured FT Qwen run. Replay without a system prompt renders successfully: Liquid/Qwen3.5 include an empty thought where their template requires one; LFM2.5 renders the answer directly. The original LFM2.5 template ignores `reasoning_content`, so the existing `--inline_think` transformation is necessary and correct for nonempty intents. Empty intents produce no inline think block on that family, a small target-format difference.
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:317:For both Qwen configs, the [pinned modeling source](https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/v5.20.2/src/transformers/models/qwen3_5/modeling_qwen3_5.py) and publisher configurations identify 24 language layers: 18 linear-attention and six full-attention. The regex from each **actual job JSON** matches all **186 intended LM linear modules** in the constructed name set:
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:331:Finally, `warmup_steps=0.03` is valid in [Transformers 5.20.2](https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/v5.20.2/src/transformers/training_args.py#L2118): values below one are fractions. It means **38 warmup steps** for 1,250 updates, or **57** for 1,875. This was not misreported as a fractional-step bug. L4 memory/time remain unmeasured: no token-length census, largest-replay-batch check or GPU smoke run was performed. `max_length=None` avoids chopping image tokens, but also permits arbitrarily expensive long examples; do not treat the current batch sizes as locally certified to fit.
