results/codex/codex_data_v2_audit.md:5:Audited dataset: `experimentalmachines/AndroidAgent-SFT-v2` at **`8e0e63a48f180aa60c103d2f492d6364355cb306`**. Downloaded exactly **three v2 train shards, 00000/00003/00004**, selected with seed `20261117`, and all three dev shards: **15,000 train + 1,999 dev = 16,999 rows**. Dataset files/card/stats totaled **1,626,522,302 bytes**. The remaining 13 train shards were not downloaded or inspected. Findings are confirmed instances or explicitly bounded sample results, not a certification of all 79,991 advertised train rows.
results/codex/codex_data_v2_audit.md:12:| F2 | **major** | **The shared type-only contract differs from the AndroidWorld executor.** The actual executor function, run with recording ADB stubs, executes `type_text("Art"), Enter, Enter` for `input_text("Art")` followed by `keyboard_enter`. **99/100** inspected AMEX Enter rows immediately follow raw `TYPE` steps. v1 has no `keyboard_enter` targets; v2 introduces this explicit second-submit pattern. [Probe](data_v2_cache/executor_probe.json), [executor](../../android_world/android_world/env/actuation.py), [protocol](../../docs/EVAL_PROTOCOL.md). | Resolve the execution contract explicitly. To retain the shared format, implement a type-only agent adapter and compare **both v1 and v2** with that adapter; keep standard-protocol AW scores separately labeled. If standard AW auto-Enter must remain, retain only trajectories whose observations/actions remain valid under it. Do not blindly delete Enter rows or fabricate intermediate screenshots. This is a pre-existing v1 mismatch that the new Enter allocation makes more consequential. |
results/codex/codex_data_v2_audit.md:13:| F3 | **major** | **Cardinal direction does not establish executable scroll semantics.** AMEX `87dde1a8dfb3407a980f2fbc9e4572ff/12` scrolls a narrow time dropdown. Raw finger path is `(946,725)→(967,1547)` on 1440×3040. The actual AW `scroll up` path is `(720,1520)→(720,3040)`, outside the dropdown. [Overlay](data_v2_cache/visual/amex_21_scroll_paths.png). Builder accepts it at `data/build_v2_mix.py:309`. | Reject region-specific scrolls, drags, and other gestures that the fixed center executor cannot reproduce, and truncate dependent history at that step. Alternatively extend and test a shared region-aware action contract in builder, trainer and executor before including them. Checking only angle and distance is insufficient. |
results/codex/codex_data_v2_audit.md:14:| F4 | **major** | **AMEX key-like text is treated as literal typing.** Five downloaded train targets are `input_text("esc")`; `53cc23e9f1c0492c900cf960c4a4a9a7/13` is a non-editable article screen. Independent reconstruction selects **17 `esc` targets and one newline-only target** before image filtering. Two inspected histories also contain newline-only typing. [Article example](data_v2_cache/visual/extra_amex_05.png), [selection](data_v2_cache/amex_selected_before_images.jsonl). | Validate `TYPE` payload semantics. Quarantine Escape-like actions and their dependent suffixes unless source execution establishes a supported equivalent. Map genuine Enter events to `keyboard_enter` only after resolving F2; preserve actual multiline text. Do not train literal `esc`, or automatically assume Escape equals Back. |
