results/codex/codex_data_v2_verify4.md:3:**Final decision: GO for training both LFM3-VL-2B and Qwen3.5-2B on `experimentalmachines/AndroidAgent-SFT-v2` @ `42f7f763649d4d2c73eeb99ff5f0bc33bd15a16a`, using the v1 recipe: 1,250 steps × effective batch 32 = 40,000 row presentations.** The two blocking conversion defects from [verification 3](codex_data_v2_verify3.md) pass this bounded re-verification. No new B1/B2 blocker was observed. The previous judgment that residual source-label noise is non-blocking is unchanged.
results/codex/codex_data_v2_verify4.md:5:Dataset: [immutable DATA revision](https://huggingface.co/datasets/experimentalmachines/AndroidAgent-SFT-v2/tree/42f7f763649d4d2c73eeb99ff5f0bc33bd15a16a). Inspected the B1/B2 patch in `cb1ffec` and the current builder at local HEAD `4c3c5a7337ee7da4cb256322cafdfa50710fc7aa`. Builder SHA-256: `d96819262789c6296fa7fe3e8079178568ef8b81f71ab4429b93f8984fc0f946`. At this HEAD, `HEAD~1` already contains the builder fix; `git show cb1ffec -- data/build_v2_mix.py` exposes the relevant change.
results/codex/codex_data_v2_verify4.md:10:| **B2 — control/selection drags emitted as generic scrolls** | **PASS within the stated scope** | All three named gesture paths fail the stricter geometry rule; actual loops cut before or at those steps. The complete published dev split contains no offending clock row or dependent suffix. Reviewed **20 published scroll rows**, ten per new source, prioritizing short/off-centre paths: **0 visible control/selection drags**. All **433** downloaded new-source scroll targets match their raw source paths and current acceptance rules. |
results/codex/codex_data_v2_verify4.md:27:For `TEXT → tap → result tap`, hide-keyboard at `[500,950]`, toolbar at `[686,499]` and suggestion at `[249,453]` retain only TEXT and cut at the tap. Genuine bottom-right Search and Enter at `[920,930]` retain TEXT plus the result, with one `input_text` history action. Negative dismissal wording overrides a bottom-right coordinate. A second submit-like tap cuts; an ordinary app tap remains. AMEX soft-key taps and explicit `PRESS_ENTER` merge correctly, and a second submit-like tap cuts. [Actual-loop fixtures](data_v2_cache/verify4_42f7f76364/actual_loop_fixtures.json).
