results/codex/codex_data_v2_verify4.md:42:For B2, reviewed **20 distinct published rows/images**, ten Odyssey and ten AMEX, ranked toward the remaining short/off-centre paths. Visible operations were list/page/gallery scrolling, launcher swipes and a scrollable calendar month grid; none dragged a clock hand, slider or text-selection handle. Also exercised real-loop fixtures rejecting drag wording, scrolling immediately after Odyssey long-press, short drags and diagonal drags, while retaining ordinary page swipes. These observations support the fix; the heuristic is not a universal proof of executor equivalence.
results/codex/codex_data_v2_verify4.md:52:| Caps / quotas | **PASS.** Full stats report maximum **3** train rows per Odyssey/AMEX episode. Observed maxima are Odyssey **3**, AMEX **3**, ScreenQA **2**; dev Odyssey **1**, AMEX **4**, ScreenQA **2**. The actual adversarial quota fixture returns **3 unique rows** from one episode across quota passes. All source totals remain below their ceilings; AMEX has **999 input_text**, **12 standalone Enter**, and AC **5,998 terminal** train rows. |
results/codex/codex_data_v2_verify4.md:58:Both jobs retain **1,250 steps, batch 8 × accumulation 4, learning rate `2e-4`, LoRA rank 64 / alpha 128, `MAX_PIXELS=774400`, and thinking-enabled training**. No builder, dataset, trainer or job was edited, and no training/device run was launched. **LFM3-VL-2B: GO. Qwen3.5-2B: GO.** This decision applies to this immutable revision and the requested v1-budget experiment.
