results/codex/codex_final_eval.md:137:The pinned dataset `1c49e7d117bd109eebd976b04deefa708b0e2007` contains **99,216 train rows / 13,573 episodes**, **827 validation rows / 137 episodes**, and the **18,415-row test**. Reading non-image columns of every shard found **zero train/val/test episode intersections**, no duplicate row keys, no IDs outside official splits, and zero GT field mismatches. Thirty official train episodes are absent; the surviving stats cannot attribute all 30 to the AW-app filter. Independently reading the source mirror's train episode IDs reproduces the cards' **1,238 official test episodes in mirror train** claim.
results/codex/codex_final_eval.md:139:No positive split-leakage evidence was found. Limits: the AW-app filter is a name heuristic; screenshot duplicates across distinct episodes and pretraining contamination were not tested. 450M replay is recorded only as `/content/data/replay`, without an archived row/image roster or source revisions proving no MMStar/MMLU overlap. Run configs record model/dataset SHAs but loading code does not pin those revisions. There is no isolated replay ablation. AC train has **13,573 positive `complete` labels and zero `answer`, `keyboard_enter` or `infeasible` labels**; that supervision gap is consistent with, but does not prove the cause of, the observed failures.
