results/codex/codex_eval_pass1.md:7:Evidence levels matter here: I independently checked local metadata, source, installed AndroidWorld changes, GGUF metadata/template, and trusted episode pickles. I exercised the production parser and summarizer with synthetic counterexamples. I checked versioned upstream TRL/Transformers source and public model sources. I did **not** run GPU training, download the private processed dataset, reproduce a phone benchmark, or recompute real AndroidControl predictions: none of those prediction files exists locally. `dataset_verification.json` explicitly says its numbers were copied from lost VM output; it is an assertion to audit, not an independently reproducible verification record.
results/codex/codex_eval_pass1.md:82:**Minor — low-mode coverage and bbox wording.** Low rows are emitted only for nonempty hints (`:206–207`). The aggregate artifact reports 8,428 low rows versus 8,444 high ordinary steps, not two complete copies. The claimed total 18,415 is consistent with `8,444 + 8,428 + 1,543`; two full copies would total 18,431. Likewise, 8,435 curated records do not mean 8,435 bbox-bearing clicks. **Fix:** publish exact per-mode manifests and the bbox-bearing denominator, and either retain blank-hint low rows with an explicit policy or identify this as a restricted low-level subset.
results/codex/codex_eval_pass1.md:108:`train/patch_qwen35_template.py:10–27` places the assistant body and end token inside generation markers, while keeping the role header outside. Its single-occurrence assertions guard against an unexpected input template. No confirmed Qwen masking defect was found. These are character/source checks, **not a tokenizer-mask dump or a live GPU forward/backward verification of the active VM**. Saving one actual masked batch and trainable-parameter listing would close that remaining assurance gap.
results/codex/codex_eval_pass1.md:274:| Lower-priority architecture/efficiency control | **SmolVLM2-2.2B-Instruct** | The [publisher card](https://huggingface.co/HuggingFaceTB/SmolVLM2-2.2B-Instruct) provides the image-capable checkpoint and tuning guidance; [llama.cpp's multimodal documentation](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/docs/multimodal.md) explicitly lists its GGUF. It is a useful portable control, not an established AndroidWorld winner. |
