results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:13:It creates a new `results/codex/pass2/repro_*` directory. Eight groups of checks passed. “Passed” means the expected counterexamples or positive controls reproduced, not that the pipeline is safe. Tests use Python/Jinja, tiny fake dataset objects, actual parser/scorer/summarizer code, AST-extracted production functions, and isolated copies of shell scripts with fake Python/upload commands. They do not start a Colab session, run a GPU model, upload anything, or download weights/datasets. Versioned upstream source was read to establish dependency behavior. Actual Arrow casting, tokenizer-level masks on model tokenizers, CUDA memory, active VM code versions, and Hub checkpoint contents were **not** validated. Character-mask and source evidence must not be described as a successful training batch.
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:63:Impact: both Qwen runs can consume GPU time after a required base measurement failed, and the chain can proceed from a failed preceding model. A green client exit is not evidence of a trained, evaluated, durably saved model.
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:108:Evidence: `vm_model_pipeline.sh:76–83` uses FT thinking 1 and base thinking 0; `docs/EVAL_PROTOCOL.md:15–18` explicitly documents this. Rendering proves these are different prompts. Qwen base is prefixed with an already closed empty think block; FT is prefixed with an open think block and must spend some of its 256 new tokens on intent and closure. LFM3 has the analogous difference. Greedy decoding alone does not make them matched comparisons.
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:191:Fix: filter/validate first and sample to an exact budget, or record and gate on the accepted count. Persist source revision/subset/shard/index, image/text hashes, transformations and exclusion counts. Include this manifest in the training identity and deduplicate against the frozen general evaluation where possible. Log both row and supervised-token mixture proportions; label the two-shard source restriction. Add a small real Arrow encode/save/load/cast and collator preflight before GPU allocation.
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:248:Evidence: `sft_vlm.py:64,103,110–113`; `generate.py:37,48–51`; `eval_general.py:32–34,69,84`; `build_general_replay.py:34–35`. Every model/dataset load uses a mutable ID or directory without an immutable revision/hash. Remote model code is trusted without recording its revision. Data loads use all files matching `data/<split>/*.parquet`; stale overlapping shards in that namespace would be concatenated. Neither training nor generation asserts processed split membership, uniqueness, raw provenance or frozen GT identity before GPU work. The source split lists are disjoint, but that alone cannot certify every later parquet upload.
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:252:Fix: produce one resolved immutable experiment manifest before GPU work, save it with checkpoints and every eval chunk, and compare it on restore/reuse. Include git/source hashes, library lock plus observed versions, model/tokenizer/processor/code revisions, dataset shard and key manifests, replay membership/transforms, templates, exact trainable names, seeds, schedule and decoding policy. Run split/duplicate/GT checks on the exact published revision. Record unknown foundation-model contamination as unknown; no audit here proves pretraining leak freedom.
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:331:Finally, `warmup_steps=0.03` is valid in [Transformers 5.20.2](https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/blob/v5.20.2/src/transformers/training_args.py#L2118): values below one are fractions. It means **38 warmup steps** for 1,250 updates, or **57** for 1,875. This was not misreported as a fractional-step bug. L4 memory/time remain unmeasured: no token-length census, largest-replay-batch check or GPU smoke run was performed. `max_length=None` avoids chopping image tokens, but also permits arbitrarily expensive long examples; do not treat the current batch sizes as locally certified to fit.
results/codex/codex_adversarial_pass2.md:358:**Required before launching the configured Qwen jobs:** make stage receipts/identities and error propagation reliable; fail closed on requested checkpoint restoration; freeze the dataset/replay/model/template/runtime manifest; use independent expected-row validation; persist evaluation progress durably; match general-eval preprocessing and specify thinking/answer parsing; predeclare a retention margin with paired uncertainty. Preserve the completed work already on the running models rather than relaunching it under an unverified identity. Separately fix AW lifecycle/summary handling before calling any downstream suite result comparable. Then run tiny real CPU processor/collator/schema checks and a separately authorized GPU smoke test before committing the full budgets. The local template/regex positives alone are insufficient to waive these blockers.
