ents with Step-Level Filtering\" (He et al., 2025).\nUnlike traditional trajectory-level filtering approaches… See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/microsoft/WebSTAR.","downloads":1232,"tags":["language:en","license:cdla-permissive-2.0","modality:image","arxiv:2512.10962","arxiv:2410.19609","region:us"],"createdAt":"2026-01-23T21:23:59.000Z","key":""},{"_id":"697a5daa1609967b26bc05dc","id":"microsoft/CancerGUIDE","author":"microsoft","disabled":false,"gated":false,"lastModified":"2026-02-06T19:45:04.000Z","likes":8,"trendingScore":0,"private":false,"sha":"7ea7be7de8fb526d92eb6ea0a4f3d27099b92831","description":"\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tDataset Card for CancerGUIDE Synthetic Patient Data\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tDataset Summary\n\t\n\nCancerGUIDE Synthetic Patient Data contains synthetically generated oncology patient profiles paired with recommended treatments. The dataset was created using GPT-4.1 following the methodology described in the CancerGUIDE paper, employing both structured and unstructured generation approaches. The resulting data serves as a benchmark for evaluating and training large language models (LLMs) in… See the full description on the dataset page: https://huggingface.co/datasets/microsoft/CancerGUIDE.","downloads":108,"tags":["language:en","license:mit","size_categories:n<1K","format:json","modality:text","library:datasets","library:pandas","library:polars","library:mlcroissant","arxiv:2509.07325","region:us","synthetic-data","oncology","llm","gpt-4.1"],"createdAt":"2026-01-28T19:04:10.000Z","key":""},{"_id":"6985b836486703d123ae8985","id":"microsoft/Verus_Training_Data","author":"microsoft","disabled":false,"gated":false,"lastModified":"2026-02-06T09:49:47.000Z","likes":9,"trendingScore":0,"private":false,"sha":"d3a283fabb152ceee6e3e350a30d37499ece4f90","description":"\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tReadme\n\t\n\nThis is our Verus training data for SAFE and VeruSyn.\n\n\t\n\t\t\n\t\n\t\n\t\tSAFE's SFT data