+**GUI datasets for v4: adversarial viability audit**
+
+Audit date: 2026-11-17. Decision scope: additions to LFM3-VL-2B under the remaining approximately 3.5 GPU-hours. **Recommendation: choose the NULL option. Admit zero rows from the nine listed releases for the next run.** Finish and validate v3, then spend the next training allocation on our own corrected histories, recovery, navigation-to-answer, and completion boundaries. This is a decision about incremental value and preparation cost, not a claim that all nine datasets lack useful content.
+
+Three potentially useful findings survived scrutiny: GUI-Reflection really contains synthetic mistakes and recovery; Libra/Aguvis reasoning really can be joined to some of our selected steps; and Libra contains factual answers missing from raw AMEX terminal labels. None established an advantage over v3 plus the proposed targeted round under this budget. OS-Genesis has direct AndroidWorld contamination, the specified Android-Lab repository is empty, this AiTZ mirror contains original test data, and Mobile-R1's released typing payloads are systematically defective.
+
+**Decision and size ledger**
+
+“Admit 0” below is the recommended allocation, not an invented estimate that every underlying row is unusable. Conditional candidate counts and unknown full-corpus yields are distinguished explicitly. Dataset names are linked to the exact audited revisions.
+
+| Dataset / pinned revision | Verdict | Observed size and sampling | Size after the proposed admission decision |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| [GUI_Reflection_SFT_train](https://huggingface.co/datasets/craigwu/GUI_Reflection_SFT_train/tree/58bca9449fc3ce46d52641a0f8e59c9da1f99313) | **REJECT** import; reuse method on our AC | Reflection filenames advertise 15K ineffective + 17K modified-goal rows. Parsed 838 + 892 rows from bounded prefixes, plus 839 + 832 modified-goal rows from two later byte windows; sampled 40 from each prefix and examined later recovery chains. Full totals not counted. | **0**. Full yield after single-image, split, package, and physical-validity filtering **UNVERIFIED**. |
+| [GUI_Reflection_Task_Suite_train](https://huggingface.co/datasets/craigwu/GUI_Reflection_Task_Suite_train/tree/df3dcc4e81ddbe92349da2d38f8cabb4c9439d69) | **REJECT** | Parsed 915 AC reversal, 3,056 AC verification, 2,319 AMEX reattempt rows; 40-row samples for each. Advertised component sizes are not verified exact totals. | **0** for our action SFT. Auxiliary classification/grounding rows are not executable recovery trajectories. |
+| [android-lab-train](https://huggingface.co/datasets/xuyifan/android-lab-train/tree/99627f2eeceb45050c23fe25b16ba7f0fd06c9d1) | **REJECT** | Only `.gitattributes` and a 31-byte license-only README; no training payload. | **0 available**. |
+| [GUI-Libra-81K-SFT](https://huggingface.co/datasets/GUI-Libra/GUI-Libra-81K-SFT/tree/05bb2c5f7e81de38f3d7826739db46913dd08a23) | **REJECT** addition; strongest future answer-label donor | Full mobile annotation scans: 19,694 AMEX + 21,234 Odyssey. 40-row samples per component; additional join samples; **40 answer endpoint images visually reviewed**. | **0 admitted**. 242 AMEX answers → **132 structural candidates**, before visual/history/executor acceptance. These have 1,166 prefix rows; 1,298 is a candidate upper bound, not a ready mix. |
+| [aguvis-stage2](https://huggingface.co/datasets/xlangai/aguvis-stage2/tree/bd6f1ed43498beb8e5474adcb2592c7d521d692e) | **REJECT** addition; possible intent-label donor | Full AMEX and Odyssey L2/L3 annotation scans: 38,469 AMEX and 118,282 Odyssey rows **per variant**; 40-row samples per component/variant. L2/L3 are alternate annotations, not twice the independent experience. | **0 admitted**. Verified joins below; complete accepted intent-replacement count **UNVERIFIED**. Other mobile components were inventoried, not equivalently audited. |
+| [xwm/AITZ](https://huggingface.co/datasets/xwm/AITZ/tree/633599cc37e81e00bb2f050d086cd9c63d191947) | **REJECT** | Viewer reports 4,724 rows; 160 fetched at four offsets, with a 40-row text review. All 160 paths identify original AiTZ **test** data. | **0** under original-split preservation. |
+| [UI-Genie-Agent-16k](https://huggingface.co/datasets/HanXiao1999/UI-Genie-Agent-16k/tree/13cf4f3e66e9bd2528f9cf080e72d7983394f27d) | **REJECT** | Repository contains both `ui_genie_agent_16k.jsonl` and `AMEX_Agent_34K.jsonl`; parsed 471 / 475 bounded-prefix rows and sampled 40 each. Names are not exact verified totals. | **0 admitted**. Full yield of factual answers with valid executable prefixes **UNVERIFIED**. |
+| [OS-Genesis-mobile-data](https://huggingface.co/datasets/OS-Copilot/OS-Genesis-mobile-data/tree/872b66a76210a43fca7c15c2b160c31829e9dc52) | **REJECT** | Viewer reports 51,114 rows. Parsed 904 `ac` + 753 `aw` prefix rows; 40-row samples each. Both contain AW examples. | **0** under exclusion of this AW-derived release. |
+| [Mobile-R1](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Mobile-R1/Mobile-R1/tree/c3904f0fdad03a3a4191492880312bda5ad36516) | **REJECT** | Full JSONL: **1,007 trajectories / 3,899 steps**; 40 trajectories sampled for text review. All 361 parsed `type` actions type literal `success`; five actions fail schema parsing. | **0 admitted**. A repaired-prefix yield is **UNVERIFIED**, and cannot be calculated merely by subtracting the 366 defective actions. |
+
+**What was actually inspected**
+
+HF metadata, cards, schemas, annotation samples, repository trees, and upstream documentation were fetched live. `HF_HOME` and download/cache paths were placed under gitignored `results/codex/v4_cache`; authentication used the existing local token without copying it into evidence. Most JSONL sampling used bounded 2 MiB windows. To answer C3 precisely, the two Libra and four Aguvis annotation files were downloaded in full, approximately **1.21 GB combined**, while avoiding their full image archives. Thus this was small media sampling, not a small total annotation transfer. Reflection's later ranges were inspected to avoid mistaking a prefix of Back labels for the entire recovery design.
+
+Sampling used seed `20261117`; random selection within a downloaded prefix is **not** a globally representative sample. Automated counts cover the stated parsed population. Text review does not establish screenshot grounding. The strongest visual pass was 40 Libra answer endpoints: matching AMEX filenames fetched by HTTP byte ranges from Aguvis's AMEX ZIP, with manifest hashes. Their content was visually inspected; **byte identity with Libra's split image archive was not verified**, and earlier trajectory states were not replayed. No emulator execution or new model training was performed in this audit.
+
+Durable counts, revision pins, join results, Mobile-R1 defects, and all 40 visual-review notes are in [dataset_viability_v4_evidence.json](dataset_viability_v4_evidence.json). Raw material and scripts are in [v4_cache](v4_cache/), particularly `sample_summary.json`, `join_summary.json`, `other_summary.json`, `libra_answer_candidate_audit.json`, `libra_answer_visual_review.json`, `audit_fetch.py`, `join_audit.py`, and `answer_candidates.py`. These cached source rows are not proposed training data.
+
+The local baseline was checked against [V2_COMPARISON.md](../V2_COMPARISON.md), [the v2 plan](../../docs/DATA_V2_PLAN.md), [the original viability audit](dataset_viability.md), the v2 audit/verification reports, and [the literature review](../../reports/Small%20GUI%20agent%20training%20methods.md). The final v2 pin is `42f7f763649d4d2c73eeb99ff5f0bc33bd15a16a`: 78,982 training rows, comprising 55,936 AC, 9,979 Odyssey, 7,072 AMEX, and 5,995 ScreenQA. Its LFM3-v1/v2 step scores are Odyssey .269/.644, AMEX .306/.735, and ScreenQA .000/.764, while AC-low .948/.893 and terminal .792/.732 declined. The user-reported AW 0/38 versus v1 15/116 is a partial, unmatched comparison, not a completed causal experiment. Blank training intents and frequent empty thoughts are a plausible defect; this audit does **not** establish that filling them alone repairs AW success.
+
+**Contract and contamination rules used in the decisions**
+
+[train/agent_format.py](../../train/agent_format.py) supplies one current screenshot, a goal, and up to eight prior text intent/action pairs. Targets contain a short intent and one JSON action. The supported actions are `click`, `long_press`, `input_text`, `scroll`, `open_app`, `navigate_back`, `navigate_home`, `keyboard_enter`, `wait`, `answer`, and `status` with `complete`/`infeasible`. Points are integer coordinates in [0,1000]. There is no arbitrary drag, separate observation-memory tool, accessibility-tree input, or index-only click in this contract.
+
+| Source operation | Exact conversion condition; reject when it fails |
+|---|---|
+| Pixel click / long press | Use actual image width/height, not a copied prompt resolution; normalize and round each coordinate to [0,1000]. Require a visible target. Do not silently clamp bad coordinates. |
+| Already normalized point | Distinguish [0,1] from [0,1000]; multiply only the former. Require the source's current image to match the row. |
+| SoM/index or bbox grounding | Resolve through original element bounds and verify the center on the raw current screenshot. An index alone is insufficient. Removing marked targets can remove information the source model had. |
+| Type / write | [AW actuation](../../android_world/android_world/env/actuation.py) types **and presses Enter**. Keep only when this compound behavior is appropriate. Coalesce an immediately following equivalent submit/Enter, with the correct next state/history; drop a field-entry prefix when auto-submit would change later states. Never retain an extra Enter by default. |
+| Swipe / scroll | Our executor swipes from the screen center toward an edge. Map **finger up → content down**, down → up, left → right, right → left, only when the source describes finger displacement. Do not invert an already content-oriented `scroll`. Reject sliders, drawing, edge pulls, regional carousels or swipes requiring a different origin. |
+| Compound action / unsupported key | Do not collapse focus+type, multiple clicks, `clear`, arbitrary keys, or multi-call code into a single action without intermediate-state evidence. Cut the dependent suffix at the first unsupported transition. |
+| Terminal | Require visible or logged state evidence that every requested operation is done. A model-authored success flag is not evidence. Failure is not automatically `infeasible`. |
+| Factual response | Map to `answer(text)` only when the goal requests information and the answer is supported by the current screenshot or causally available text history. [Our AW agent](../../eval/androidworld/lfm_agent.py) ends the episode on `answer`; do not append a terminal row afterward. |
+| Reasoning / history | Retain a short, grounded intent, not arbitrary long CoT. Rebuild history using only past information available to this executor. Dropping past images, trees, memory, or generated observations is lossy unless the target remains supported. Wrong past actions may be context, never successful-action targets. |
+
+Contamination has three separate levels: shared app family; use of AW environment/task initialization; and duplication of benchmark goal templates/seeds. These must not be conflated. The exclusion list is Simple Calendar, Simple SMS, Simple Draw, Simple Gallery, Markor, Pro Expense, Broccoli, Joplin, OsmAnd, Retro Music, VLC, Tasks (`org.tasks`), Audio Recorder, and OpenTracks, including package variants. Representative package checks are `com.simplemobiletools.calendar.pro`, `com.simplemobiletools.smsmessenger`, `com.simplemobiletools.draw.pro`, `com.simplemobiletools.gallery.pro`, `net.gsantner.markor`, `com.arduia.expense`, `com.flauschcode.broccoli`, `net.cozic.joplin`, `net.osmand*`, `code.name.monkey.retromusic`, `org.videolan.vlc`, `org.tasks`, `com.dimowner.audiorecorder`, and `de.dennisguse.opentracks`.
+
+Use the actual [v2 package rules](../../data/build_v2_mix.py), plus explicit package verification, not a name-only substring filter. Google Tasks is not automatically `org.tasks`; Android-Lab's Calendar is `com.skuld.calendario`, not Simple Calendar. Shared Settings/Clock/browser screens are not themselves proof of AW task leakage. All new episodes must also be disjoint from our dev/test episode IDs and images; unknown provenance is not evidence of cleanliness.
+
+**1. craigwu/GUI_Reflection_SFT_train — REJECT the import; use the recovery construction idea**
+
+**Terms/provenance.** MIT on the dataset card; the card explicitly sends users to upstream AndroidControl, AitW/AiTZ, AMEX, and Odyssey for images. That is an annotation license declaration, not a blanket replacement for upstream terms. AMEX/Odyssey declare CC BY 4.0. AndroidControl has an unresolved documentation inconsistency discussed below. The two sampled reflection components identify AndroidControl; all 838 ineffective and 892 modified-goal prefix rows map to official AC train episodes.
+
+**Actual supervision and C1.** The recovery behavior is real in the annotations:
+
+| Source locator | Observed input and target | What it establishes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `sft_reflection_ineffective_15k.jsonl`, line 1, `episode_10004_1.png` | Busuu notifications goal; history clicks the already-selected Me area; last image is repeated. Target `CLICK[[940,87]]` opens settings and its thought recognizes no screen change. | Synthetic no-op recognition followed by a different action. |
+| `sft_reflection_modify_goal_17k.jsonl`, line 1, `episode_0_3.png` | Goal asks for upcoming Zoho meetings; history chose Past; target `CLICK[[165,162]]` selects Upcoming. | Goal-conditioned correction. |
+| Same file, line 25, `episode_10060_5.png` | Eurostar refund-policy task; mistaken train-information popup; target `PRESS_BACK`. | Explicit corrective Back. |
+| Same file, row beginning at byte 21,001,936, episode 603 | Image sequence `603_0,603_1,603_0`; mistaken Filter action, Back in history, then `CLICK[[764,152]]` for Brand. | Wrong tap → Back → retry, not merely isolated Back labels. |
+| Same file, row beginning at byte 40,002,625, episode 15911 | Image sequence `15911_0,15911_1,15911_2,15911_1`; wrong amenities action, Back, then reviews at `[187,660]`. | A second later-file recovery chain. |
+
+**Conversion and loss.** Original sampled rows have **2–5 images**, prior actions, optional memory, a thought, an action description, and an action. A current corrective click/Back can be represented in our action space, but copying only the last image discards comparison evidence. `MEMORIZE` has no direct equivalent. The [paper's construction](https://arxiv.org/html/2506.08012) assumes Back restores an earlier screenshot and inserted ineffective actions leave it unchanged; these are synthetic transitions, not verified physical rollouts. Keep the distinction even when the story sounds plausible. One sampled modified-goal row, line 177 / episode 10467, rationalizes an already-sent email and proceeds to compose another; this is not a general reversible-mistake guarantee.
+
+**Contamination and size.** No evidence these offline reflection samples were generated in AW. However, an AC source tag does not exclude all 14 app families; full package/template screening was not completed. Verified official-train membership of the prefixes is narrower than corpus-wide split safety. Filename 15K/17K counts are approximate; the number that would survive one-image and executor screening is **UNVERIFIED**.
+
+**Decision.** This is the best match for measured loops/no-ops and corrective intents, but the same construction on our already-selected AC rows avoids importing multi-image assumptions and mixed source histories. It does not provide our model's own failure-state distribution or calibrated completion. C1 is **VERIFIED for synthetic mistake/recovery content; CONDITIONAL for single-screenshot usability; UNVERIFIED for physical transition validity**. Allocate zero external rows.
+
+**2. craigwu/GUI_Reflection_Task_Suite_train — REJECT**
+
+**Terms/provenance.** MIT card; upstream AC, Odyssey, AMEX, **OS-Atlas-desktop**, and WaveUI images. OS-Atlas-desktop in this card is not evidence that its mobile examples came from AW. Upstream terms still apply.
+
+**Rows and format.** AC reversal line 1 uses `episode_6163_2/3.png`, two screenshots, six textual choices, and an explanation plus answer letter D for a reverse scroll. AC verification line 1 uses `episode_2823_2/3.png` and a Yes label for whether typing Pittsfield worked. AMEX reattempt line 1 presents a Home target, supplied wrong red boxes, and bbox `[0,945,200,997]`. These supervise reversal classification, before/after verification, and retry grounding with privileged mistake markings. Their “Answer” labels are not factual responses to an app user's query.
+
+**Conversion/loss and quality.** Two-image classification cannot become a one-image next action merely by renaming labels. A bbox center could become a click only after reconstructing goal, failed history, raw screenshot, and valid bounds; red-box feedback is absent from our runtime. Multiple-choice labels have no executor meaning. The observed issue is task mismatch, not proof that the source annotations are wrong. There is no verified execute-fail-correct sequence or terminal calibration in these sampled training tasks.
+
+**Contamination/size/decision.** AC/AMEX/Odyssey derivative overlap and app/template provenance require the same checks as their sources; full 14-family coverage is **UNVERIFIED**. Advertised filenames include AC/Odyssey reversal 4K each, verification 32K/31K, and AMEX/OS-Atlas/WaveUI reattempt 41K/39K/20K; these are not independent mobile trajectories or verified exact counts. Admit **0**. A separate auxiliary verifier/grounder objective is outside this v4 action-SFT budget.
