+**7. HanXiao1999/UI-Genie-Agent-16k — REJECT for this run**
+
+**Terms/provenance.** MIT card. The primary file contains generated agent trajectories associated with the Android-Lab setting; the separate AMEX file inherits AMEX's upstream conditions. The [official project](https://github.com/Euphoria16/UI-Genie) distinguishes its agent trajectories from its large reward-model dataset. The latter's negative/reward supervision cannot be attributed to this Agent-16k release. These are another policy's histories, not LFM3's own on-policy data.
+
+**Row evidence.** Of 471 complete primary-file prefix rows, 67 terminate, 43 type, 40 swipe, and 55 contain SoM/index-style targets requiring additional grounding. All 471 referenced image paths exist in the repository tree; that does not verify pixels or action correctness. The assistant emits a `mobile_use` call with `action_desc`, generally without a separate thought. Some `action_info` values really are factual answers:
+
+| 1-based JSONL line | Observed label | Assessment |
+|---|---|---|
+| 5 | Calculator task 89−56; terminal `action_info` gives 33. | Factual endpoint exists; do not claim this release has no answers. |
+| 25 | Bluecoins category query reports Family Activities not found. | Potential negative query answer; correctness needs screen/state checking. |
+| 61 | Calendar query reports no Parent Teacher Conference event. | Potential navigation-to-answer endpoint. |
+| 62 | Budget query reports $0.00, while `action_desc` says the budget has been successfully set. | Query-versus-mutation semantic drift; an unsafe intent donor. |
+| 247 | Goal adds a Bluecoins grocery expense; click description says Open Clock. | Clear goal/description mismatch. |
+| 427 | Goal asks current timer duration and how to change it; action clears the current timer. | Query-versus-action ambiguity needing review. |
+
+Line 1's wait duration also disagrees with its description (two versus three seconds). These examples disprove a blanket “all terminals are trustworthy” interpretation; they do not estimate a corpus-wide error rate.
+
+**Conversion and loss.** One screenshot and textual progress fit our shape better than multi-image Reflection, but SoM indices need original bounds and a raw-screen grounding check. Pixel coordinates must use actual image dimensions. `type` still has the auto-Enter issue; `swipe` can require a noncentral origin. Map Back/Home/Enter only from supported system buttons, reject Menu/arbitrary `key`/clear operations, and reject dependent suffixes. Extract a short intent from a validated `action_desc`, not unconditionally. Convert a factual `action_info` to `answer` only after verifying the goal and evidence; a generic success status maps to neither factual answer nor proven completion by itself.
+
+**Contamination/size/decision.** Android-Lab's Calendar is a different package from Simple Calendar, and its Bluecoins/Maps.me/Pi Music apps are not Pro Expense/OsmAnd/Retro Music. This is evidence against careless name-based contamination claims, not a full clean bill: exact AW task-template and all-package overlap are **UNVERIFIED**. Neither the 16K name nor the additional 34K filename is a verified count of accepted trajectories. Factual endpoints are a real lead, but reconstructing valid prefixes, SoM targets, and goal-consistent intents costs more than this audit has established is worthwhile versus our own targeted round. Admit **0**; full filtered yield **UNVERIFIED**.
+
+**8. OS-Copilot/OS-Genesis-mobile-data — REJECT; C4 VERIFIED**
+
+**Terms/provenance.** MIT dataset card. The [collection README](https://github.com/OS-Copilot/OS-Genesis/blob/main/collection/README.md) explicitly instructs collection in AndroidWorld's emulator with its installed apps. The [random-walk code](https://github.com/OS-Copilot/OS-Genesis/blob/main/collection/random_walk_aw.py) loads the AW environment, enumerates `ANDROID_WORLD_FAMILY`, generates task parameters, and calls `task.initialize_task(env)` before exploration. Its app mapping includes all 14 named third-party families. This is verified reuse of AW infrastructure and task initializations, stronger than merely sharing generic Android apps. Exact duplication of held-out natural-language goals/seeds remains **UNVERIFIED**.
+
+**Rows.** Both `os_genesis_ac_training_data.jsonl` and `os_genesis_aw_training_data.jsonl` begin with `aw_stage1_task1_1`, a Tasks due-date goal. The `ac` file also contains Simple Calendar at line 25, Broccoli at line 63, Pro Expense around line 292, VLC around line 352, Simple Draw around line 552, Markor around line 597, and SMS around line 600. The `aw` sample includes Retro Music and OpenTracks. Therefore **dropping only the file named `aw` does not remove AW data**. Names and `aw_` IDs are visible row evidence; the generator confirms why they occur.
+
+**Format and quality.** Rows combine a screenshot, accessibility-tree text, goal/history, and either reasoning-plus-action or an action conditioned on a supplied thought. One such task3 variant is not an independently observed trajectory. Removing the tree can remove target indices or focus information. Actions resembling our JSON still need point normalization, status translation, and focus/type semantics; index/focus+type cannot become a single equivalent input without evidence. Some sampled app openings conflict with their goals, so contamination is not the only concern. A synthetic success label is not an external outcome check.
+
+**Failure coverage/size/decision.** This release can contain reasoning and correction-like content, but its AW state familiarity would confound the intended held-out evaluation. The viewer reports 51,114 rows, not 51,114 complete trajectories. Admit **0 from the release**. No attempt was made to certify an uncontaminated residual based only on file names; exact-template overlap has not been measured. C4 is **VERIFIED**, without claiming every row duplicates an AW benchmark prompt.
